The embedding layer converts each token into a vector representing its general semantic meaning. These embeddings are then passed to the Transformer.
Inside the Transformer, the self-attention mechanism compares each token's embedding with the embeddings of all other tokens in the input. Based on these relationships, it updates the embeddings into contextual embeddings,
allowing the model to understand the correct meaning of each word within the specific sentence before predicting the next token.


[Embeddings provide the starting meaning. Self-attention refines that meaning using the context of the entire prompt.]


